The primary preterm-piglet study directly reports that neither dopamine nor dobutamine increased cardiac output or cerebral blood flow. A second neonatal piglet study provides useful nuance: dopamine increased heart blood flow in preterm animals, but did not significantly alter cerebral or other measured organ flows there; dobutamine’s brain-flow increase was in term, not preterm piglets. I’ll check the evidence graph for existing matching records before adding these findings.

